<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Heinrich X Reuss of Lobenstein</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1621">1621</a>–<a href="/years/1671">1671</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Heinrich X was a count of the Younger Line of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-reuss">House of Reuss</a>, which named all its male members Heinrich. In the division of 1647 he received <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bad-lobenstein">Lobenstein</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thuringian-highlands">Thuringian Highlands</a>, founding the line of Reuss-Lobenstein. His sons later divided his lands, creating the branches of Ebersdorf and Hirschberg.</p></div>
